<title>USA: DH Technology Inc Q1 oper shr falls.</title>
<headline>DH Technology Inc Q1 oper shr falls.</headline>
<dateline>SAN DIEGO, Calif. 1997-04-23</dateline>
<text>
<p>Three Months Ended March 31,	1997	    1996</p>
<p> Net sales			     $19,185	$28,196</p>
<p>  Cost of net sales		   12,527	 18,470</p>
<p>  Gross margin			   6,658	  9,726</p>
<p>Operating expenses:</p>
<p>Selling, general</p>
<p>    and administrative		 3,963	  3,960</p>
<p>   Research and development	  1,451	  1,288</p>
<p>In process technology,</p>
<p>intangible assets,</p>
<p>acquisition integration</p>
<p>    and other charges		 11,290	     --</p>
<p> Total operating expenses	   16,704	  5,248</p>
<p> Income from operations	  ( 10,046)	  4,478</p>
<p> Interest income (net)		   381	    284</p>
<p> Income before income taxes     ( 9,665)	  4,762</p>
<p> Income taxes			 ( 1,782)	  1,727</p>
<p> Net income			   ( 7,883)	  3,035</p>
<p> Net income per share		( 0.95)	   0.36</p>
<p> Shares used			     8,274	  8,469</p>
<p>		  (In Thousands, except per share amounts)</p>
<p>NOTE: Excluding non-recurring charges, first quarter net income was $0.13 per share.  After non-recurring charges, the net loss for the period was $7.9 million or $0.95 per share, compared with net income of $3 million, or $0.36 per share, in the same period last year.  During the quarter, the Company incurred a non-cash, pre-tax in-process research and development charge of $2.5 million and a one-time, pre-tax integration charge of $1.2 million related to the Company's acquisition of the assets of the card reader business of American Magnetics Corporation (AMC) announced on April 3, 1997. Additionally, DH Technology took a one-time, non-cash charge, in the quarter, of $7.5 million related to the write down of intangible assets from the acquisition of Cognitive Solutions in 1994.</p>
</text>
